  "id": "Compound::DB00774 - Gene::23632",
  "verbalization": "Hydroflumethiazide, a thiazide diuretic, is implicated in the relationship with Ca14 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydroflumethiazide binds to multiple calcium-binding sites (Ca7, Ca9, and Ca12), which are all involved in the Carbonate Dehydratase Activity. This activity is a key enzymatic process that contributes to the regulation of calcium homeostasis. The shared participation in this activity by Ca14 across different binding sites indicates a potential functional link between Hydroflumethiazide and Ca14, likely through a common enzymatic pathway. The cumulative scores from the three paths support a robust, mechanistically plausible connection, emphasizing the role of Carbonate Dehydratase Activity in mediating this relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of calcium-dependent enzymatic processes in the biological effects of Hydroflumethiazide.",
